1. POLICY & GOVERNANCE
1.1 Purpose & Strategic Scope
This Standard Operating Procedure establishes definitive operational, engineering, food safety, administrative, and inventory governance over raw material storage, ingredient scaling, digital batch tracking, recipe integrity, thermal validation, and recipe modifications across all central manufacturing facilities and retail bakery outlets of the Jang-Jang Bakeshop network and Kingdom Confectionary Business Lines.
1.2 Mandatory Operational Directives & Non-Negotiable Prohibitions
Core Policy Directive: "No Official Batching Without Prior Administrative Formulation Approval & Costing."
1. Strict Prohibition on Unbatched Raw Material Ordering:
   * Bakery outlets (Laurice Delicacies – Bakerohan D.C. and Pan de Verde – Communal D.C.) and station bakers are categorically barred from ordering, requisitioning, or receiving unbatched bulk commodities (such as 25 kg flour sacks, bulk unweighed sugar, or bulk shortening slabs) directly from warehouse storage.
   * All raw materials released into production must arrive exclusively as pre-formulated, unitized, sealed batch kits scaled and certified by the Ingredient Batching Preparer (Romeo B. Malusay).
2. Prohibition of Floor Formula Modifications & Off-Book Baking:
   * Outlet bakers and production personnel are strictly forbidden from baking any bread, bun, pastry, or delicacy lacking prior written approval and official recipe costing from Central Administration.
   * Off-book flour blending, hydration tampering, sweetness adjustments, fat substitutions, unauthorized dough fermentation tweaking, or running unauthorized test batches using company inventory is strictly prohibited.
   * No unapproved baked product may be placed on retail sales display counters without corporate pricing, approved packaging, and formal administrative clearance.
3. Mandatory Multi-Tier Evaluation Gateway:
   * Every commercial formulation must complete administrative yield costing, mechanical capacity and thermal profiling, rheological dough analysis, and cGMP/food safety compliance review prior to commercial scheduling.
4. Mandatory Recipe Matching Mandate:
   * No ingredient will be scaled, sieved, or issued unless matched directly to an active code in the Official Master Formulation Register (e.g., Biscocho BIS-001, Otap OTP-001, or officially approved outlet bread lines).
5. Physical Access Restriction & Controlled Ingress:
   * Raw materials remain segregated in designated warehouse storage rooms (Dry Room 1, Cold Room, Wet Room) under the sole custody of Jade Q. Dela Cruz. Outlet bakers are prohibited from entering warehouse storage rooms.
   * Material handoffs occur exclusively through the warehouse staging Dutch door/counter. Pre-batched recipe kits enter production strictly through the Medium Care (Grey) Zone transfer airlock.
6. Zero Concealment Policy:
   * Any process drift, batch scaling discrepancy, thermal breach, mechanical anomaly, or formula defect must be logged immediately. Concealment of deviations triggers immediate progressive disciplinary action.
