	5. QUALITY AUDITING, NON-CONFORMANCE & DISCIPLINARY SANCTIONS
5.1 Quality Governance & Random Floor Audits
      1. QA Inspectors and Operations Management conduct regular, unannounced floor audits across plant stations and retail outlets (Laurice Delicacies and Pan de Verde).
      2. Audits cover:
      * Verification of scaled dough piece weights and dough exit temperatures (26°C–28°C).
      * Verification of oven core lethality probes (CCP-1: core temperature ).
      * Audit of terminal transaction hashes, station hydration logs, and shift reconciliation sheets.
      * Physical inspection of outlet storage areas to confirm total absence of unbatched bulk raw ingredients or unauthorized additives.
5.2 Quarantine & Non-Conformance Protocol (Form-NCR-001)
         1. Immediate Tagging: Any dough batch mixed without an authorized Form-ING-001 log, containing unapproved ingredient substitutions, or failing thermal lethality standards must be halted immediately and affixed with a physical RED "QUARANTINE" TAG via Form-NCR-001.
         2. Financial Loss Allocation: The full ingredient cost, packaging waste, and labor/utility overhead of the condemned batch will be charged directly as an operational loss to the offending outlet or production line cost center.
         3. Condemnation & Disposal: Quarantined products must never be reworked, blended, or salvaged without written authorization from both the Head of Administration and the FSCO & QA Control Director.
5.3 Progressive Disciplinary Policy
Violations of batching governance, unauthorized formula tweaking, off-book baking, or concealment of deviations will be penalized under SOP-HR-ORI-002 and Article 297 of the Philippine Labor Code:
         * First Offense: Documented Written Warning, formal corrective counseling, and mandatory unpaid retraining on centralized material governance.
         * Second Offense: Final Written Warning and immediate suspension without pay pending a formal administrative inquiry conference.
         * Third Offense: Escalation to the Head of Administration and HR Directorate for formal termination of employment on grounds of willful disobedience and gross neglect of duty.
